def toggle_middle_bits(n):
        # Initialize the result with 0
        result = 0 
        # Iterate over the bits starting from the second bit and ending at the second last bit
        for i in range(2, 2 ** n.bit_length() - 1):
                if i % 2 == 0:
                    # Toggle bit if its position is even
                    result |= (1 << i)
        # Combine the middle bits with the original number and remove the first and last bit
        return (n << 1) | result | ((n >> 1) & ((1 << n.bit_length() - 2) - 1))
```

