The function takes three parameters `r`, `g`, and `b` representing the RGB values. It first normalizes the RGB values to the range [0, 1]. Then it finds the maximum and minimum RGB values, which represent the saturation and value (brightness) of the color, respectively. It calculates the difference between the maximum and minimum values to determine the intensity of the color. If the maximum value is 0, the hue value is 0; otherwise, it calculates the hue based on the direction of the difference between the other two values. The saturation is calculated by dividing the difference by the maximum value and multiplying by 100. The brightness is calculated by multiplying the maximum value by 100. The function finally returns a tuple containing the hue, saturation

