The provided function works by using a heap queue algorithm to find the nth super ugly number. It initializes a hash table to track the numbers that have been generated and a min heap with the first number 1. It then enters a loop that continues until the nth super ugly number is found. In each iteration, it pops the smallest number from the heap, adds it to the hash table, and pushes all possible products of the popped number with the primes array into the heap. This process continues until the nth super ugly number is found.

